{{!-- The steading header's clock: the season Stonetop is in, over the campaign year.

      Its own partial because the header wraps it in a <button> for a GM (who can correct
      it) and a plain <div> for everyone else — two wrappers, one readout, and the partial
      is what keeps them from drifting apart.

      Two centred rows at the far right of the header: the season's name bare above, the
      year alone inside the chip below. Only the year is boxed, so the chip reads as the
      campaign's count and the name above it as the label on that count, rather than both
      competing inside one border. The name carries the season entirely on its own — bold,
      and in that season's ink (the --stonetop-season-*-ink tokens), by way of a modifier
      class interpolated from the SEASON_IDS key rather than picked by a chain of {{#if}}s:
      the value is already the token's name.

      Both halves always render. A world that has never recorded a Seasons Change is in the
      season it opened in, so the readout falls back on Spring of the First Year rather
      than showing half a clock — see DEFAULT_SEASON in module/seasons/current-season.js,
      which is also where that fallback stops: it is what the header SAYS, never what the
      steading stores. --}}
<span class="steading-header-season-name steading-header-season-name--{{season.season}}">{{season.label}}</span>
<span class="steading-header-season-year stonetop-year-chip">{{season.yearLabel}}</span>
